 qui lui servait de modèle","1938 F 257","Oil on canvas","65.2 × 50.5 cm",49],[135984360,"Le Retour du Golgotha",1856,0,null,null,0,"b/b5/Le_Retour_du_Golgotha_Paul_Delaroche.jpg/330px-Le_Retour_du_Golgotha_Paul_Delaroche.jpg",0,0,1,0,62,"Le Retour du Golgotha (Titre original)","95.22","Oil on canvas","27 × 52.9 cm",49],[135984413,"Marie-Madeleine se rendant à Marseille",1834,0,null,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,62,"Marie-Madeleine se rendant à Marseille (Titre original)","001.9.1","Oil on cardboard","19.6 × 42 cm",39],[136455399,"Saint Georges et le dragon, esquisse",1829,0,null,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,1,null,"RFML.PE.2024.4.1","Oil on canvas","28 × 23.5 cm",39],[136483365,"Cardinal Mazarin dying",1830,0,null,null,0,"7/74/Cardinal_Mazarin_Dying.jpg/330px-Cardinal_Mazarin_Dying.jpg",0,0,1,0,22,null,null,"Oil on canvas","57 × 97 cm",49],[139418200,"Napoléon à Fontainebleau, 31 mars 1814",1845,0,null,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,63,null,null,"Oil on canvas","68 × 52 cm",39],[141446005,"Charlemagne traverse les Alpes au Mont-Cenis",null,0,null,null,0,"8/8f/Charlemagne_traverse_les_Alpes_au_Mont-Cenis_d%C3%A9fendu_par_les_Lombards_en_773_gerome_Delaroche.jpg/330px-Charlemagne_traverse_les_Alpes_au_Mont-Cenis_d%C3%A9fendu_par_les_Lombards_en_773_gerome_Delaroche.jpg",0,9,1,0,null,null,null,null,null,49]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":3,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"1213453":["The Execution of Lady Jane Grey is an oil painting by Paul Delaroche, completed in 1833, which is now in the National Gallery in London.","The Execution of Lady Jane Grey"],"1224572":["Bonaparte Crossing the Alps is an 1848–1850 oil painting by French artist Paul Delaroche.","Bonaparte Crossing the Alps"],"2959421":["Charles I Insulted by Cromwell's Soldiers is an oil painting by the French artist Paul Delaroche, depicting Charles I of England taunted by the victorious soldiers of Oliver Cromwell after the Second English Civil War, prior to his execution in 1649.","Charles I Insulted by Cromwell's Soldiers"],"12901163":["Napoleon I at Fontainebleau on March 31, 1814 is an oil on canvas painting by the French painter Paul Delaroche, created in 1840. Not coincidentally, the work was made in the same year that the Retour des cendres, or the return of Napoleon's mortal remains from the island of Saint Helena took place.","Napoleon I at Fontainebleau on March 31, 1814"],"16915832":["The Young Martyr is an oil painting by the French painter Paul Delaroche. It was completed in 1855 and is based on the Romantic style of genre painting.","The Young Martyr"],"17174298":["The Assassination of the Duke of Guise is an oil-on-canvas painting by French artist Paul Delaroche, created in 1834. It is held in the Musée Condé, in Chantilly, whilst a replica hangs in the Château de Blois.","The Assassination of the Duke of Guise (Delaroche)"],"17176901":["Cromwell Opening the Coffin of Charles I is an oil on canvas painting by Paul Delaroche from 1831. It can be seen in the Musée des Beaux-Arts de Nîmes.","Cromwell Opening the Coffin of Charles I"],"17190332":["The Children of Edward is an oil on canvas painting by French painter Paul Delaroche, created in 1830. It is held in the Louvre, in Paris.","The Children of Edward"],"17631000":["Joan of Arc, Sick, Interrogated in Prison by the Cardinal of Winchester is an oil on canvas painting by French painter Paul Delaroche, created in 1824.","Joan of Arc, Sick, Interrogated in Prison by the Cardinal of Winchester"],"27813772":["Saint Amelia, Queen of Hungary is an oil painting by Paul Delaroche, from 1831 to 1834. It was investigated in 2016 by the BBC TV programme Fake or Fortune?, and is held in a private collection.","Saint Amelia, Queen of Hungary"],"50084065":["The State Barge of Cardinal Richelieu on the Rhône is an 1829 history painting by the French artist Paul Delaroche. It depicts the state barge of Cardinal Richelieu on the River Rhône in Southern France.","The State Barge of Cardinal Richelieu on the Rhône"],"88982350":["Saint Cecilia and the Angels is an oil on canvas religious painting by the French artist Paul Delaroche, from 1836. It depicts Saint Cecilia, the Christian Roman martyr and patron saint of music, accompanied by two angels.","Saint Cecilia and the Angels"],"104444944":["The Victors of the Bastille in Front of the Hôtel de Ville is a large oil on canvas painting by French painter Paul Delaroche, from c. 1835. It is held in the Petit Palais, in Paris.","The Victors of the Bastille in Front of the Hôtel de Ville"],"112264336":["The Duke of Angoulême at the Taking of Trocadero is an 1828 oil-on-canvas painting by the French painter Paul Delaroche. Combining elements of portraiture and history painting, it shows Louis Antoine, Duke of Angoulême during the Battle of Trocadero on 31 August 1823.","The Duke of Angoulême at the Taking of Trocadero"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}